      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Look around you; the system is designed for committees, for compromise, for the slow accretion of political vanity. In 2035, that sluggishness is a vulnerability, a systemic failure against complex global threats. AI-driven governance isn't about removing humanity; it's about optimizing it, allowing objective, data-driven logic to replace partisan inertia. We can achieve true stability and efficiency only when policy is calibrated to demonstrable outcomes, not electoral whims.\"",
