      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"The critique that the algorithm is merely a vessel for bias misses the fundamental truth: human judgment is already biased. Every elected official, no matter how sincere, operates through an imperfect lens of fear, tribalism, and self-interest. My system doesn't lack ethics; it quantifies them. It strips away the messy, subjective scaffolding of human emotion to prioritize observable, measurable good. Math, in its purest form, offers a standard of consistency that human morality can only perpetual dilute.\"",
      "source": "target",
